# Sanar, Unfinished Genius "enters prepared" (CR 722.3a): its Wild Idea copy is in exile and Sanar is prepared. On turn 3 Bot1 casts
# that copy for {3}{U}{R} (five Moxen), which unprepares Sanar (CR 722.3d) and finds an instant or sorcery card: Plains is refused as
# a find (beside the positive control, Lightning Bolt), which goes to Bot1's hand. The copy ceases to exist after resolving. Casting
# it was casting a sorcery spell, so Sanar's "Activate only if you've cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn" is satisfied and
# {T} makes a Treasure token (Sanar has been Bot1's since turn 1, so the {T} is not summoning-sick).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Sanar, Unfinished Genius
Plains
Plains
Lightning Bolt
Plains x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sanar, Unfinished Genius.Cast
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sanar, Unfinished Genius.Prepared = true
? Exile = Wild Idea
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Wild Idea.Cast
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Search(Lightning Bolt)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sanar, Unfinished Genius.Prepared = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sanar, Unfinished Genius.Activate
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Plains; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Sanar, Unfinished Genius.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
